button" class="launch-cta" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-wallet" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19 7V4a1 1 0 0 0-1-1H5a2 2 0 0 0 0 4h15a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v4h-3a2 2 0 0 0 0 4h3a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-2a1 1 0 0 0-1-1"></path><path d="M3 5v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h15a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-4"></path></svg>Connect wallet<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down wallet-menu-caret" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></div></div></header><div id="page-content" class="app-content"><article class="hk-doc hk-card"><header class="hk-doc-head"><p class="hk-kicker"><span>[--]</span><span>Legal</span><i></i><span>Updated <!-- -->31 Oct 2026</span></p><h1>Terms of service</h1></header><div class="hk-doc-body"><p>These Terms of Service (“Terms”) govern your access to and use of hokori.io and any related websites, interfaces, data feeds, tools, content and features that we make available (together, the “Services”). The Services are operated by <strong>Ad Hok Development LLC</strong>, a Wyoming limited liability company (“Hokori”, “we”, “us” or “our”). Please read these Terms carefully before using the Services. They replace any earlier agreement, representation or understanding about your use of the Services. If you do not agree to all of these Terms, you must not use the Services.</p><p><strong>THESE TERMS CONTAIN DISCLAIMERS OF WARRANTIES, LIMITATIONS OF LIABILITY, RELEASES, A CLASS-ACTION WAIVER, A JURY-TRIAL WAIVER AND A REQUIREMENT TO RESOLVE ALL CLAIMS BY BINDING INDIVIDUAL ARBITRATION (SECTIONS 25 TO 27). THEY APPLY TO CLAIMS AGAINST HOKORI AND ITS AFFILIATES, MANAGERS, MEMBERS, SERVICE PROVIDERS, PARTNERS, ADVISORS AND VENDORS (TOGETHER, THE “COVERED PARTIES”), WHO ARE EXPRESS THIRD-PARTY BENEFICIARIES OF THE ARBITRATION PROVISIONS. THESE PROVISIONS ARE AN ESSENTIAL BASIS OF THIS AGREEMENT.</strong></p><p>You accept these Terms in full when you do any of the following: (a) access or use the Services; (b) connect a wallet to the Services; (c) create, buy, sell or otherwise transact in any digital asset through the Services; or (d) convert or stake HOKORI through the Services.</p><h2 id="definitions">1. Definitions</h2><ul><li><strong>“Smart Contracts”</strong> means the self-executing programs on public blockchains that the Services let you interact with, including Hokori’s launch factory, bonding curves, fee vaults and liquidity lockers on Starknet; the HOKORI token, locker, conversion gateway, staking contract and fee splitter on Starknet; and the HOKORI conversion program on Solana. Their addresses are listed on the Transparency page.</li><li><strong>“User-Created Coin”</strong> means any digital asset created by a user through the Services.</li><li><strong>“HOKORI”</strong> means the HOKORI token (ticker HKR) on Solana (“Solana HOKORI”) and its one-for-one counterpart on Starknet (“Starknet HOKORI”).</li><li><strong>“Wallet”</strong> means a self-custodial blockchain wallet that you control.</li><li><strong>“EVM Wallet”</strong> means a Wallet made for Ethereum and compatible networks whose Ethereum key controls a Starknet account of its own through the Services.</li><li><strong>“Network Fees”</strong> means the fees charged by a blockchain network (for example Starknet or Solana) to process a transaction. They are paid to the network, not to Hokori.</li><li><strong>“Applicable Laws”</strong> has the meaning given in Section 19.</li></ul><h2 id="what">2. What Hokori is, and what it is not</h2><p><strong>2.1 Software.</strong> Hokori provides software: a website and related tools that let you interact directly with the Smart Contracts on Starknet to create digital assets, buy and sell them, and claim fees, and, for HOKORI, to convert and stake it.</p><p><strong>2.2 Non-custodial.</strong> We never hold, control or have access to your Wallet, its private keys or recovery phrase, or your digital assets. Every transaction is prepared in your browser, approved by you in your Wallet, and settled by the relevant blockchain. We cannot reverse, cancel or change a transaction once you have submitted it.</p><p><strong>2.3 Not a financial institution.</strong> Hokori is not a broker, dealer, exchange, trading venue, custodian, money transmitter, investment adviser, fiduciary or financial institution of any kind, and is not registered or licensed as one in any jurisdiction. We do not match orders, set prices, execute trades on your behalf or act as your agent. Prices are set by the Smart Contracts and by other users’ trading. Nothing in our relationship creates any fiduciary or other duty to you beyond those expressly stated in these Terms.</p><p><strong>2.4 No endorsement.</strong> We do not create, issue, sponsor, review, endorse or verify User-Created Coins, their creators, or anything said about them, and we do not recommend buying, selling or holding any digital asset.</p><p><strong>2.5 No advice.</strong> Nothing on the Services is financial, investment, legal, tax or other professional advice. You are solely responsible for deciding whether any transaction is right for you. Consider consulting your own advisers.</p><h2 id="eligibility">3. Eligibility</h2><p>You may use the Services only if you can form a legally binding contract under the laws that apply to you and you are at least eighteen (18) years old, or the age of majority where you live if that is higher. If you use the Services for an entity, you confirm that you are authorized to bind it and that it is duly organized, validly existing and in good standing under the laws of the place where it is organized. If you are a Prohibited User (Section 4) or do not meet these requirements, you do not have permission to use the Services. We may refuse or end anyone’s access to the Services at any time, for any reason, in our sole discretion.</p><h2 id="prohibited-users">4. Prohibited Users</h2><p>The Services are not available to: (i) individuals or entities (including those owned or controlled by individuals) that are the subject of economic or trade sanctions administered or enforced by any governmental authority, or that are otherwise designated on any list of prohibited or restricted parties (including those maintained by the United Nations Security Council, the European Union, His Majesty’s Treasury of the United Kingdom (the “UK Treasury”) and the U.S. Department of the Treasury); (ii) individuals or entities placed on the Denied Persons List by the Bureau of Industry and Security of the U.S. Department of Commerce; or (iii) residents or citizens of, or entities located in or organized under the laws of, any country, territory or region subject to a U.S. Government embargo, designated by the U.S. Government as a terrorist-supporting country, or otherwise subject to comprehensive country-, territory- or region-wide sanctions by the United Nations, the European Union, the UK Treasury or the United States, including Cuba, the Crimea, Donetsk and Luhansk regions of Ukraine, Iran, North Korea, Russia, Syria and Yemen (together, “Prohibited Users”).</p><h2 id="prohibited-access">5. Prohibited Access</h2><p>You may not access the Services with a Jail-Broken Mobile Device, a Rooted Android Device or the substantial equivalent. A “Jail-Broken Mobile Device” is a mobile device running Apple’s iOS whose software restrictions have been removed by any procedure not authorized by Apple. A “Rooted Android Device” is a device running Android on which privileged root access has been enabled.</p><p>Access to the Services is also prohibited to persons and entities of any jurisdiction in which using the Services, or holding or transacting in digital assets, is prohibited by law. You must not use a VPN, proxy, location spoofing or any other means to hide your location, identity or Wallet in order to get around these restrictions.</p><h2 id="requirements">6. Wallet, digital asset and technology requirements</h2><p>You are responsible, at all times and at your own cost, for obtaining and maintaining:</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding-left:8px"><li>(a) the devices, an up-to-date web browser, internet access and any other equipment, software and communications services needed to use the Services, and for making sure they are compatible;</li><li>(b) a self-custodial Starknet Wallet that works with the Services (currently Braavos, Ready and OKX Wallet), or an EVM Wallet that works with the Services (currently Phantom, MetaMask and Robinhood Wallet); we may add or remove supported wallets at any time;</li><li>(c) STRK, the Starknet network’s token, to pay Network Fees and to buy coins; and</li><li>(d) to convert HOKORI, a Solana Wallet holding Solana HOKORI and enough SOL to pay Solana Network Fees.</li></ul><p>We do not guarantee that the Services can be used on every device, through every network or wireless plan, in every browser, or in every location. Network Fees, data charges and similar costs may apply and are your sole responsibility. A transaction that fails on chain may still cost Network Fees.</p><p>You assume all risks of using internet-based blockchain networks, including risks relating to hardware, software and internet connections, the introduction of malicious software, and unauthorized access by third parties to information stored on a blockchain or in your Wallet. Digital assets, cryptocurrencies and blockchain technology are relatively new, and the law that applies to them is unsettled.</p><h2 id="security">7. Your Wallet and its security</h2><p>You alone control your Wallet and are responsible for keeping its private keys, recovery phrase and passwords secure. We will <strong>never</strong> ask for your private key, recovery phrase or one-time codes, and you must never share them with anyone who asks, including anyone claiming to be Hokori. Anyone who gains access to your Wallet can move your assets, and we cannot recover them. Check every transaction your Wallet asks you to approve. Please report suspected impersonation of Hokori, or a suspected security problem with the Services, to security@hokori.io.</p><h2 id="creating">8. Creating a coin</h2><p><strong>8.1 Your choices.</strong> When you create a coin, you choose its name, ticker, image, description and links, and up to five fee recipients and their shares. The Smart Contracts create the coin in your transaction, and you may buy the first tokens in the same transaction. Every coin’s address ends in “dab”. The Services may show additional information about the coin, including the signals described in Section 14.</p><p><strong>8.2 Permanent content.</strong> Your coin’s image and details are uploaded from your browser to Arweave, a public, permanent storage network that we do not control. Once uploaded, they cannot be changed or deleted by you or by us. We can only choose whether the Services display them (Section 13).</p><p><strong>8.3 Your responsibility for what you publish.</strong> You are solely responsible for every image, name and word you publish with your coin. Because uploads are permanent, check them before you launch. You confirm that you have every right needed to publish them and that they comply with Section 13.</p><p><strong>8.4 Child sexual abuse material.</strong> You must never upload, or use as or with a coin, any child sexual abuse material or any image that sexualizes a minor, in any form, including drawn, edited, synthetic or AI-generated images. We screen uploads, and where we find such material we report it to the appropriate authorities as the law requires, preserve the related records and cooperate with law enforcement. Doing so is a serious crime in most jurisdictions.</p><p><strong>8.5 Promoting your coin.</strong> Anything you say or publish about your coin, on the Services or elsewhere, must be accurate and not misleading, and you must disclose your own holdings and interest when you promote it. Any arrangement to share fees with other people is solely between you and them. Fees paid to recipients depend on trading, the Smart Contracts and the network, and we do not guarantee any amount. You are responsible for any taxes on fees you receive.</p><h2 id="trading">9. Trading, graduation and transactions</h2><p><strong>9.1 The bonding curve.</strong> A new coin trades on its own bonding curve, a Smart Contract whose formula sets the price: the price rises as tokens are bought and falls as they are sold. The minimum trade is 0.1 STRK.</p><p><strong>9.2 Estimates and limits.</strong> Before you sign, the Services show an estimate of the result, including the price impact of your trade. You set a slippage limit: your trade executes within that limit or fails. The Smart Contracts, not the Services, determine the actual result, which may differ from the estimate.</p><p><strong>9.3 Graduation.</strong> When every token offered on a coin’s curve has been bought, the coin graduates: its liquidity moves to a pool on Ekubo, a third-party protocol on Starknet, where it is locked permanently by the Smart Contracts, and trading continues there.</p><p><strong>9.4 Transactions are final.</strong> Blockchain transactions cannot be reversed. A transaction may fail, be delayed or execute at a different time than you expect, for reasons including network congestion, other users’ transactions submitted before yours (sometimes called front-running), changes in Network Fees, and outages of wallets, networks or providers. We do not guarantee that any transaction will execute, or execute at any particular price or time.</p><h2 id="fees">10. Fees</h2><p>Coins launched through Hokori’s launch factory pay the following fees, which are set in its Smart Contracts and collected by them automatically:</p><ul><li><strong>Trading fee:</strong> 0.9% of every buy and sell. 85% of it goes to the coin’s fee recipients, chosen by its creator, and 15% to Hokori.</li><li><strong>Graduation fee:</strong> 1% of the curve’s reserve when a coin graduates, divided the same way.</li><li><strong>Launch window:</strong> buys in the block in which a coin is created, and in the next block, pay a fee of 99%, to discourage automated sniping.</li><li><strong>No launch fee.</strong></li><li><strong>Network Fees</strong> are paid to the network, not to Hokori.</li></ul><p>The fees for coins launched through a factory are fixed in its Smart Contract and cannot be changed for those coins. Hokori’s share goes to Hokori’s fee splitter contract. The current figures and every contract address are on the Transparency page.</p><h2 id="conversion">11. HOKORI conversion</h2><p>Starknet HOKORI exists only as a one-for-one counterpart of Solana HOKORI. The entire Starknet supply of 1,000,000,000 HOKORI was created once and placed in a locker contract, and nothing can create more. To convert, you burn Solana HOKORI through the conversion program on Solana, naming your Starknet address. When two of Hokori’s three independent attester keys have confirmed that the burn is final, the same amount is released from the locker to that address.</p><ul><li><strong>Irreversible.</strong> Burned Solana HOKORI is destroyed. There is no way to convert Starknet HOKORI back to Solana HOKORI.</li><li><strong>Check the destination.</strong> Coins credited to a wrong address cannot be recovered.</li><li><strong>Timing and limits.</strong> Conversion depends on the attester services, the networks and their providers, and may be delayed. A burn above the conversion limits in force is held for manual review before it is credited. We may pause conversion, for example during a security incident or where the law requires it. We will make reasonable efforts to credit every valid burn, but we do not guarantee when.</li><li><strong>No market from Hokori.</strong> Hokori does not operate a market for Starknet HOKORI. Solana HOKORI trades on third-party venues that we do not control, and we do not guarantee the value or liquidity of HOKORI on any network.</li></ul><h2 id="staking">12. Staking</h2><p>There is no communication regarding staking. No offer is made, and no agreement is formed, that could form the basis of an investment contract. Staking is optional and at your sole discretion.</p><h2 id="content">13. Content, moderation and intellectual property</h2><p><strong>13.1 Your content.</strong> You keep ownership of the names, images, descriptions, links and profile details you submit (“Your Content”). You grant Hokori a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, perpetual and irrevocable licence to host, store, reproduce, display, distribute and make Your Content available, and to let our service providers do so, as needed to operate, display, promote and improve the Services. The licence is perpetual because content on Arweave is permanent.</p><p><strong>13.2 Prohibited content.</strong> You must not create, name, describe or illustrate a coin or profile with content that:</p><ul><li>sexualizes or exploits a minor in any way, or depicts child sexual abuse (Section 8.4);</li><li>depicts gore, cruelty or graphic violence, or glorifies violence or terrorism;</li><li>is pornographic or sexually explicit;</li><li>harasses, threatens or incites hatred against a person or group, or promotes hate symbols;</li><li>reveals someone’s private information, or impersonates a person, company or project;</li><li>infringes a trademark, copyright or other right; or</li><li>is otherwise unlawful where Hokori is operated or where you are.</li></ul><p><strong>13.3 Moderation.</strong> We screen uploaded images automatically and may review content. We may decline to display any coin, image, profile or other content on the Services, at any time and without notice, including where we reasonably believe this Section is breached, where we receive a credible report, or where the law requires it. This does not change the coin or its Smart Contracts on chain, and we are not required to explain our decisions. Where the law requires it, we report apparent child sexual abuse material to the appropriate authorities and preserve related records. We cooperate with lawful requests from law enforcement. Report content to abuse@hokori.io.</p><p><strong>13.4 Copyright and trademark complaints.</strong> If you believe that content shown on the Services infringes your copyright or trademark, email abuse@hokori.io with: (a) a description of the work or mark; (b) where it appears on the Services (the coin’s address or the page’s link); (c) your name, address, telephone number and email address; (d) a statement that you believe in good faith that the use is not authorized by the owner, its agent or the law; (e) a statement that the information in your notice is accurate and, under penalty of perjury, that you are the owner or authorized to act for the owner; and (f) your physical or electronic signature. We may stop displaying the content and may tell the person who published it. Because coin content is stored permanently on Arweave, we can stop displaying it on the Services but cannot remove it from Arweave. We may stop displaying content from, and restrict access to the Services by, anyone who repeatedly infringes others’ rights.</p><p><strong>13.5 Our intellectual property.</strong> The Services, including their software, design, text, graphics, logos and the Hokori name, belong to Hokori or its licensors. We grant you a limited, revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use the Services for your own use in line with these Terms. You may not use the Hokori name or logos in a way that suggests our endorsement without our written permission.</p><h2 id="info">14. Information shown on the Services</h2><p>The Services show prices, charts,