acts run on public blockchains, the digital assets in your Wallet remain yours and can be used through other interfaces even if the Services are unavailable to you.</p><h2 id="investment">17. Not an investment</h2><p><strong>USER-CREATED COINS AND HOKORI ARE NOT INVESTMENT OPPORTUNITIES, INVESTMENT CONTRACTS OR SECURITIES OF ANY KIND.</strong></p><p>By using the Services, you acknowledge and agree that you are not acquiring any digital asset in the expectation of profit from the efforts of Hokori or any other person. Digital assets on the Services may be extremely volatile, and you may lose everything you spend. We make no statement that any digital asset will rise in value or keep its value. No content on the Services is, or should be taken as, advice, a recommendation, or an invitation to enter into any agreement for investment purposes, and no part of the Services is an offer of securities or other financial products in any jurisdiction.</p><p><strong>IT REMAINS YOUR SOLE RESPONSIBILITY TO MAKE SURE THAT YOUR USE OF THE SERVICES AND YOUR TRANSACTIONS IN DIGITAL ASSETS COMPLY WITH THE LAWS OF YOUR JURISDICTION AND OF ALL APPLICABLE JURISDICTIONS. ALL TRANSACTIONS ARE FINAL AND NON-REFUNDABLE.</strong></p><p>We have no responsibility or liability for any digital assets that are lost, misplaced or inaccessible.</p><h2 id="taxes">18. Taxes</h2><p>You are solely responsible for determining, reporting and paying any taxes that apply to your use of the Services, including on trades, fees you receive as a creator or fee recipient, conversions, staking, and any other amount you receive.</p><h2 id="laws">19. Compliance with laws</h2><p>There are rules, regulations and laws that address digital assets and blockchain technology (“Emerging Technology Laws”), and they may be adopted by any U.S. state or other jurisdiction, inside or outside the United States. You are also subject to all municipal, state and federal laws, rules and regulations of the places where you live and from which you access the Services (together with Emerging Technology Laws, “Applicable Laws”). You agree to comply with, and are solely responsible for complying with, all Applicable Laws. You acknowledge that your use of the Services is at your own risk, and that we are not responsible if any Applicable Law restricts or prohibits your access to the Services or your ability to transact in any digital asset.</p><h2 id="third">20. Third-party services</h2><p>The Services rely on, and may link to, services we do not control, including the Starknet and Solana networks; Ekubo; Arweave and its upload service; wallets; blockchain data providers; Cloudflare; price sources; content-screening providers; social media; and, for Solana HOKORI, third-party trading venues, bridges and on-ramps. We do not endorse them and are not responsible or liable for their terms, privacy practices, content, availability, security, fees or actions, or for any loss arising from your use of them. Your use of any third-party service is subject to its own terms.</p><p><strong>WE DISCLAIM ANY LIABILITY FOR THE PRICE, MARKET CONDITIONS OR TRADING VOLUME OF ANY DIGITAL ASSET ON THIRD-PARTY VENUES; FOR LOSS OF FUNDS OR DIGITAL ASSETS FROM TECHNICAL ERRORS, HACKS OR OTHER SECURITY BREACHES OF THIRD-PARTY SERVICES; AND FOR ANY DECISION BY A THIRD-PARTY VENUE, INCLUDING LISTING, DELISTING OR RESTRICTING TRADING IN ANY DIGITAL ASSET.</strong></p><h2 id="risk">21. Assumption of risk</h2><p>Digital assets, and memecoins in particular, can lose all their value quickly, and most do. Smart Contracts can contain bugs. Networks can be congested, halted or changed. Wallets, devices and accounts can be compromised. Laws and regulations may change in ways that affect digital assets, the Services or your ability to use them. You understand and accept all of these risks, and those described on the Risks page, which forms part of these Terms. You assume full responsibility for any disruption or other problem affecting the Starknet or Solana networks, and we do not guarantee the functionality, transferability or future availability of any digital asset.</p><h2 id="warranties">22. Disclaimer of warranties</h2><p><strong>THE SERVICES, THE SMART CONTRACTS AND ANY DIGITAL ASSETS ARE PROVIDED “AS IS” AND “AS AVAILABLE”. TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, ALL WARRANTIES, WHETHER EXPRESS, IMPLIED OR STATUTORY, ARE DISCLAIMED, INCLUDING ANY WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, NON-INFRINGEMENT, AND FREEDOM FROM VIRUSES OR OTHER HARMFUL CODE. IN PARTICULAR, WE DO NOT WARRANT THAT THE SERVICES, THE SMART CONTRACTS, ANY DIGITAL ASSET OR ANY BLOCKCHAIN: (A) WILL MEET YOUR REQUIREMENTS; (B) WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED, TIMELY, SECURE OR ERROR-FREE, OR THAT DEFECTS WILL BE CORRECTED; (C) WILL BE FREE OF VIRUSES OR OTHER HARMFUL COMPONENTS; (D) WILL BE PROTECTED SUFFICIENTLY AGAINST INTERFERENCE OR INFRINGEMENT; (E) WILL RESULT IN ANY INCOME, REVENUE OR OTHER FINANCIAL OUTCOME; OR (F) WILL BE ACCURATE OR RELIABLE. THEY MAY CONTAIN BUGS, ERRORS AND OTHER LIMITATIONS. NO ADVICE OR INFORMATION, ORAL OR WRITTEN, CREATES ANY WARRANTY NOT EXPRESSLY STATED IN THESE TERMS. YOU ACKNOWLEDGE THAT YOU HAVE NOT RELIED ON ANY REPRESENTATION OR WARRANTY BY US OR ANYONE ACTING FOR US.</strong></p><h2 id="liability">23. Limitation of liability</h2><p><strong>TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, WE SHALL NOT BE LIABLE TO YOU OR ANY THIRD PARTY FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, PUNITIVE, ENHANCED OR EXEMPLARY DAMAGES, INCLUDING DAMAGES FOR LOSS OF PROFITS, STATUTORY DAMAGES, GOODWILL, USE, DATA OR OTHER INTANGIBLE LOSSES, EVEN IF WE HAVE BEEN ADVISED OF THEIR POSSIBILITY, ARISING FROM: (A) THE USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE THE SERVICES, THE SMART CONTRACTS OR ANY DIGITAL ASSET; (B) ANY TRANSACTION, INCLUDING ONE THAT FAILS, IS DELAYED OR EXECUTES DIFFERENTLY FROM WHAT YOU EXPECTED; (C) UNAUTHORIZED ACCESS TO YOUR WALLET OR DEVICES; (D) ANY MA