including creators, buyers, sellers and fee recipients of any coin, are solely between you and them. To the fullest extent permitted by law, you release Hokori and the other Covered Parties from all claims, demands and damages of every kind, known and unknown, arising out of or in any way connected with any such dispute. This release does not cover a claim arising from our own breach of these Terms.</p><h2 id="arbitration">25. Governing law and arbitration</h2><p><strong>25.1 Governing law.</strong> These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Delaware, without regard to its conflict-of-law principles.</p><p><strong>25.2 Arbitration.</strong> You, Hokori and the Covered Parties agree to resolve by binding arbitration all claims and disputes that arise under or relate to the Services or these Terms, including their breach, interpretation, validity or scope. Arbitration will take place before JAMS in Delaware, under its then-current commercial arbitration rules.</p><p><strong>25.3 Informal resolution first.</strong> Before starting arbitration, the party raising a dispute must send the other a written notice describing the dispute and the relief sought (to contact@hokori.io for us, or to the contact details we have for you), and both parties will try in good faith to resolve it informally for thirty (30) days after the notice is received.</p><p><strong>25.4 Time limit.</strong> To the extent the law allows, any claim must be brought within one (1) year after the facts giving rise to it first arose, or it is permanently barred. The time limit is suspended while the informal resolution in Section 25.3 is under way.</p><p><strong>25.5 Opting out.</strong> You may opt out of arbitration by emailing contact@hokori.io, with your Wallet address and a statement that you opt out of arbitration, within thirty (30) days after you first accept these Terms. If you opt out, disputes will be resolved in the state or federal courts located in Delaware, and the class-action waiver in Section 26 still applies to the extent the law allows.</p><p><strong>25.6 Scope.</strong> The arbitrator has exclusive authority to decide all questions about the scope, validity, enforceability and arbitrability of this agreement to arbitrate, except that a court decides whether the class-action waiver in Section 26 is enforceable.</p><p><strong>25.7 If the class-action waiver fails.</strong> If the class-action waiver in Section 26 is found unenforceable for a particular dispute, this agreement to arbitrate does not apply to that dispute, which will instead be decided in the state or federal courts located in Delaware. The rest of this Section continues to apply to every other dispute. These arbitration provisions survive the end of these Terms.</p><h2 id="class-waiver">26. Class-action waiver</h2><p>To the extent permitted by law, you agree that you will not bring, join or participate in any class action lawsuit as to any claim, dispute or controversy that you may have. You agree to the entry of injunctive relief to stop such a lawsuit or to remove you as a participant in it, and to pay the attorneys’ fees and court costs that Hokori incurs in seeking such relief. This provision (i) does not waive any of your rights or remedies to pursue a claim individually, and not as a class action, in binding arbitration as provided above; and (ii) is an independent agreement.</p><h2 id="jury">27. Jury-trial waiver; no sale-of-goods convention</h2><p><strong>FOR THE PURPOSES OF ANY COURT PROCEEDINGS, YOU AGREE THAT ANY DISPUTE SHALL BE TRIED BEFORE A JUDGE AND NOT A JURY, AND YOU WAIVE ANY RIGHT TO A TRIAL BEFORE A JURY. THE UNITED NATIONS CONVENTION ON CONTRACTS FOR THE INTERNATIONAL SALE OF GOODS DOES NOT APPLY TO THESE TERMS OR TO ANY TRANSACTION UNDER THEM.</strong></p><h2 id="california">28. California residents</h2><p><strong>IF YOU ARE A CALIFORNIA RESIDENT, YOU WAIVE ALL RIGHTS UNDER SECTION 1542 OF THE CIVIL CODE OF CALIFORNIA, AND ANY SIMILAR LAW OF ANY STATE OF THE UNITED STATES, AS AGAINST THE COVERED PARTIES. SECTION 1542 READS: “A GENERAL RELEASE DOES NOT EXTEND TO CLAIMS THAT THE CREDITOR OR RELEASING PARTY DOES NOT KNOW OR SUSPECT TO EXIST IN HIS OR HER FAVOR AT THE TIME OF EXECUTING THE RELEASE AND THAT, IF KNOWN BY HIM OR HER, WOULD HAVE MATERIALLY AFFECTED HIS OR HER SETTLEMENT WITH THE DEBTOR OR RELEASED PARTY.”</strong></p><p>Under California Civil Code Section 1789.3, California residents may file grievances and complaints with the Complaint Assistance Unit of the Division of Consumer Services of the California Department of Consumer Affairs, 400 R Street, Suite 1080, Sacramento, CA 95814; by phone at 916-445-1254 or 800-952-5210; or by email to dca@dca.ca.gov.</p><h2 id="privacy">29. Privacy</h2><p>Our Privacy page explains what information the Services process and why, and forms part of these Terms. Blockchain transactions, including your Wallet address and its activity, are public and permanent by nature, and we cannot change or delete them.</p><h2 id="amend">30. Changes to these Terms</h2><p>We may amend these Terms, and the Services, at any time without notice to you. The amended Terms will be posted on the Services with an updated “Last updated” date, and you should review them each time you use the Services. By continuing to use the Services, you agree to be bound by the Terms in effect at that time.</p><h2 id="contact">31. Contact and notices</h2><p>Questions: contact@hokori.io. Content reports: the Report button on a coin’s page, or abuse@hokori.io. Security reports and suspected impersonation: security@hokori.io. Official announcements are made only on Hokori’s official X account, <strong>@HOKORI_QUANTUM</strong>, and on the Services. Formal legal notices to us must be sent by email to contact@hokori.io. We may give you notice through the Services, by posting on our official X account, or through other reasonable means.</p><h2 id="general">32. General</h2><p>If any part of these Terms is held invalid or unenforceable, that part will be interpreted consistently with Applicable Law to the extent possible, and the rest remains in full force and effect. These Terms govern all use of the Services and take precedence over anything inconsistent in or associated with the Services. Our failure to enforce any provision is not a waiver of it or of the right to enforce it later. These Terms do not create any agency, partnership, joint venture or employment relationship. You may not assign or transfer your rights under these Terms without our written consent; we may assign ours. We are not liable for any delay or failure caused by events beyond our reasonable control. Provisions that by their nature should survive the end of your use of the Services will survive. If these Terms are translated, the English version prevails.</p></div><div class="hk-doc-actions"><a href="/" class="hk-back" aria-label="Back"><span aria-hidden="true"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="7.5,2.5 4,6 7.5,9.5"></polyline></svg></span>Back</a></div></article></div><div class="app-content hk-footer-wrap"><footer class="hk-footer"><div class="hk-footer-top"><div class="hk-footer-brand"><div class="hk-footer-logo"><button type="button" class="hok-flower" aria-label="Scatter the flower seeds" title="Scatter the seeds" style="width:36px;height:36px"><canvas aria-hidden="true" style="left:-36px;top:-36px;width:108px;height:108px"></canvas></button><strong>Hokori<span>.io</span></strong></div></div><nav class="hk-footer-links" aria-label="Footer"><div><h2>Product</h2><ul><li><a href="/">Trade</a></li><li><a href="/launch">Launch a coin</a></li><li><a href="/transparency">Transparency</a></li></ul></div><div><h2>Learn</h2><ul><li><a href="/about">About Hokori</a></li><li><a href="/risks">Risks</a></li></ul></div><div><h2>Legal</h2><ul><li><a href="/terms">Terms of service</a></